{% doc %}
  blocks/tabs.liquid

  A strip of tab buttons and the panel one of them shows.

  ## The strip is empty in the markup

  Each nested **Tab** renders a `role="tabpanel"` carrying `data-tab-label`, and
  `<tab-group>` in `assets/tabs.js` builds the buttons from those labels.

  This is not a shortcut, it is the only shape that works.
  `{% content_for 'blocks' %}` produces one stream of output, and the buttons
  and the panels have to end up in two different containers — the rail on one
  side, the panels on the other. No Liquid emits nested blocks twice. Either the
  buttons are generated from the panels, or the merchant types every tab name a
  second time into this block's settings and keeps two lists in sync by hand.

  With JavaScript off every panel stays visible and stacks. All of the content
  is reachable; only the switching is missing.

  ## Nothing here is FAQ-specific, and none of the shell is this file's

  The same block holds a size guide, a spec table or a set of care instructions.
  The markup is `snippets/tab-group.liquid` — the rail, the marker, the panel
  area and the ARIA wiring — which was written generic and, until now, called
  from nowhere. This is its first caller, so the strip in a section and the
  strip in the mega menu are one implementation with one set of bugs.

  ## A note on the range settings below

  Shopify validates every `range` for `(max - min) / step <= 101`, and a range
  that fails it does not fail alone: the schema is rejected whole and *every*
  setting in this block reads as undefined, so the first thing that breaks is a
  section preset elsewhere reporting an unrelated setting as missing. **Track
  corners** was `0..999 step 1` and produced exactly that — a preset complaining
  that `strip_style` did not exist. Both radius sliders now stop at 50, which is
  a pill at any strip height this component produces.

  ## Vertical and horizontal are a grid, not two layouts

  `assets/header.css` reads `.tabs--vertical` and `.tabs--horizontal` and puts
  the rail beside the panels or above them. Below 990px the vertical rail
  becomes a horizontal scroller on its own, because a column of tab names on a
  phone spends the whole screen width on labels and leaves the panel below the
  fold.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  assign orientation = s.direction | default: 'vertical'
  assign rail_width = s.rail_width | default: 260 | plus: 0
  assign gap = s.gap | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign marker_radius = s.marker_radius | default: 50 | plus: 0

  comment
    Two properties, not one, and for the reason `snippets/group.liquid` sets
    out at length: `flex` only means anything to a flex *item*, and this block
    is one only when the section it sits in lays its children out in a flex
    container — which the FAQ section does and a plain container does not. Each
    option writes both, they agree, and neither context is a special case.

    Fill is the default because a tab strip that hugs its longest tab name is a
    panel that changes width as the customer moves between tabs.
  endcomment
  if s.width == 'fit'
    assign width_flex = '0 0 auto'
    assign width_size = 'fit-content'
  else
    assign width_flex = '1 1 0%'
    assign width_size = '100%'
  endif

  comment
    The line around each tab button. `none` is a zero width rather than
    `border-style: none`, so the buttons keep the same box either way and
    choosing None does not resize the strip.
  endcomment
  assign tab_border_style = s.tab_border_style | default: 'solid'
  assign tab_border_width = 0
  if tab_border_style != 'none'
    assign tab_border_width = s.tab_border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0
  endif

  assign tabs_id = 'Tabs-' | append: block.id

  comment
    ## Plain and Segmented are one strip with a track drawn round it

    Segmented is the pill chooser — a filled track, the tabs sharing its width,
    the marker sliding inside it. It is a modifier and not a second component
    because everything that makes a tab strip work is already here: the measured
    marker, the keyboard walk, the overflow scroller, the ARIA. What changes is
    a background, a padding and how the tabs divide the space.

    It is the arrangement a delivery-frequency chooser wants, and equally a
    Monthly/Yearly price switch or a two-state filter — so it is a look this
    block offers rather than something a section grows its own copy of.

    Segmented is horizontal by definition: a filled track running down the side
    of a page with the options stacked in it is a menu, not a switch. The
    orientation is forced rather than hidden behind a `visible_if`, so a
    merchant who chooses Segmented on a strip that was vertical gets the strip
    they picked instead of a broken one.
  endcomment
  assign strip_style = s.strip_style | default: 'plain'
  if strip_style == 'segmented'
    assign orientation = 'horizontal'
  endif

  comment
    `tabs` and `tabs--<orientation>` are the snippet's. This is the modifier
    list on top of them, which is why it does not repeat either.
  endcomment
  assign classes = 'tabs--block'
  if strip_style == 'segmented'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' tabs--segmented'
  endif
  if orientation == 'vertical' and s.show_divider
    assign classes = classes | append: ' tabs--divided'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture tabs_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
  --tabs-rail-width: {{ rail_width }}px;
  --tabs-gap: {{ gap }}px;
  --tabs-marker-radius: {{ marker_radius }}px;
  {%- if strip_style == 'segmented' -%}
    --tabs-track-padding: {{ s.track_padding | default: 6 | plus: 0 }}px;
    --tabs-track-radius: {{ s.track_radius | default: 999 | plus: 0 }}px;
    {%- if s.track_background != blank -%}
      --tabs-track-background: {{ s.track_background }};
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if s.marker_background != blank -%}
      --tabs-marker-background: {{ s.marker_background }};
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  --tabs-flex: {{ width_flex }};
  --tabs-width: {{ width_size }};
  --tabs-tab-border-width: {{ tab_border_width }}px;
  {%- if tab_border_width > 0 -%}
    --tabs-tab-border-style: {{ tab_border_style }};
    {%- if s.tab_border_color != blank -%}
      --tabs-tab-border-color: {{ s.tab_border_color }};
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Captured, because the shell has to wrap it. `blocks/section-header.liquid`
  hands its children to `snippets/group.liquid` the same way: a block stream is
  a string once it is captured, and a snippet can put a string anywhere.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture panels -%}
  {% content_for 'blocks' %}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture tab_attributes -%}
  data-block-spacing {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The animation wraps the strip rather than replacing it: `<tab-group>` has to
  be the custom element `assets/tabs.js` defines, so the one that animates goes
  around it and takes the width with it — a wrapper that did not would leave the
  strip sized to its content inside a full-width box.

  Its two targets are the rail and the panels, so **Stagger between items** means
  the tab names arrive and then what they open. Staggering the wrapper against
  itself would be one element with a delay on it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<motion-effect
  class="tabs-motion"
  style="--tabs-flex: {{ width_flex }}; --tabs-width: {{ width_size }};"
  {% render 'motion-attrs', kind: 'text', block: s, target: '.tabs__rail, .tabs__panels' %}
>
  {% render 'tab-group',
     id: tabs_id,
     panels: panels,
     orientation: orientation,
     classes: classes,
     label: s.label,
     styles: tabs_style,
     attributes: tab_attributes %}
</motion-effect>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.tabs.name",
  "tag": null,
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "_tab" }
  ],
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.layout" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "strip_style",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.strip_style.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.strip_style.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "plain", "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.strip_style.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "segmented", "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.strip_style.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "plain"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "track_background",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.track_background.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.strip_style == 'segmented' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "marker_background",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.marker_background.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.strip_style == 'segmented' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "track_padding",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.track_padding.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 24,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 6,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.strip_style == 'segmented' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "track_radius",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.track_radius.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.track_radius.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 50,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.strip_style == 'segmented' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "direction",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.direction.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.direction.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "vertical", "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.direction.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "horizontal", "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.direction.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "vertical",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.strip_style != 'segmented' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "rail_width",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.rail_width.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.rail_width.info",
      "min": 140,
      "max": 400,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 260,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.direction == 'vertical' and block.settings.strip_style != 'segmented' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_divider",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.show_divider.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.show_divider.info",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.direction == 'vertical' and block.settings.strip_style != 'segmented' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.gap.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 80,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "width",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.width.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.settings.width.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "fill", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.width.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "fit", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.width.options__1.label" }
      ],
      "default": "fill"
    },

    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.label.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.label.info"
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:shared.appearance.header" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "tab_border_style",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.tab_border_style.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.tab_border_style.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "solid", "label": "t:shared.options.solid" },
        { "value": "dashed", "label": "t:shared.border.style.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "solid"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "tab_border_width",
      "label": "t:shared.border.thickness.label",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.tab_border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "tab_border_color",
      "label": "t:shared.border.color.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.tab_border_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "marker_radius",
      "label": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.marker_radius.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.tabs.settings.marker_radius.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 50
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:shared.animation.header" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "animation_text",
      "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "inherit", "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "fade-in", "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "fade-up", "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "slide-up", "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_text.options__5.label" }
      ],
      "default": "inherit"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "animation_duration",
      "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_duration.label",
      "info": "t:shared.animation.animation_duration.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 2000,
      "step": 100,
      "unit": "ms",
      "default": 1000,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.animation_text != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "animation_stagger",
      "label": "t:shared.animation.animation_stagger.label",
      "info": "t:shared.animation.animation_stagger.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 300,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "ms",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.animation_text != 'none' }}"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:shared.spacing.block_header" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "padding_device",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "desktop", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "mobile", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.tabs.name",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "_tab",
          "settings": { "label": "First tab" }
        },
        {
          "type": "_tab",
          "settings": { "label": "Second tab" }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
